{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5df","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0762f-28c8-71f3-b2cc-60a7b5a2a367"},"sequence":330,"recorded_at":1780531400000655,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"ce1e892e-3ef2-41ae-9338-dcad9ed9c1ee","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"ce1e892e-3ef2-41ae-9338-dcad9ed9c1ee","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"ce1e892e-3ef2-41ae-9338-dcad9ed9c1ee"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"26d7f7bb-52e2-4fe2-8b76-66147798d51e"},"task_id":"26d7f7bb-52e2-4fe2-8b76-66147798d51e","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"26d7f7bb-52e2-4fe2-8b76-66147798d51e","chunk":"Read text file `internal/environ/measure_agreement_test.go`.\n1|package environ\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"fmt\"\n5|\t\"strings\"\n6|\t\"testing\"\n7|\n8|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/canonicaljson\"\n9|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/dirnode\"\n10|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/provhost\"\n11|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n12|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/sessadapter\"\n13|)\n14|\n15|// This file is the cross-facade string-measure battery. Section\n16|// 1.6 bounds strings in characters, not bytes: string[1..128]\n17|// admits 128 characters of any width. Two strict decoders both\n18|// blind to lone surrogates was one drift class the cross-story\n19|// review found; byte-vs-rune bounds disagreeing on a member that\n20|// crosses both protocols was another. This battery pins the\n21|// measure at every character-bound member one facade shares with\n22|// another, with multibyte vectors that separate the measures: a\n23|// 128-`é` value is 128 characters but 256 bytes, so a\n24|// byte-measure refuses what the specification admits.\n25|//\n26|// The byte side is ledgered, not left open. Provider SpawnPlan\n27|// argv elements and totals and env-literal values bound BYTES by\n28|// Section 5.1 (outside this story), implemented in exactly two\n29|// functions — provhost checkSpawnArgv and checkSpawnEnvLiterals\n30|// — and the byte rows below drive all three byte gates through\n31|// the production DecodeSpawnPlan entry. validEnvName measures\n32|// len() over an ASCII-only grammar where bytes and runes\n33|// coincide, so no row can separate them; that is stated here,\n34|// not hidden. Every other string bound in the census scope flows\n35|// through the single measure helper of its package (census\n36|// ledger: StringLength, runeLength, stringLength), and the rune\n37|// rows pin the helper verdicts at one crossing member per\n38|// facade plus every provhost rune site.\n39|\n40|// validSpawnJSON is one valid Provider SpawnPlan body with the\n41|// given profile mapping, first extra argv element, literal value,\n42|// and native session ID literal. The argv always carries one\n43|// short flag so element-count rules hold while one member under\n44|// test varies.\n45|func validSpawnJSON(mapping, extraArgv, literalValue, nativeID string) []byte {\n46|\targv := `[\"--serve\"]`\n47|\tif extraArgv != \"\" {\n48|\t\targv = fmt.Sprintf(`[\"--serve\",%s]`, jsonQuote(extraArgv))\n49|\t}\n50|\tliterals := `{}`\n51|\tif literalValue != \"\" {\n52|\t\tliterals = fmt.Sprintf(`{\"EXTRA_KEY\":%s}`, jsonQuote(literalValue))\n53|\t}\n54|\tnative := `null`\n55|\tif nativeID != \"\" {\n56|\t\tnative = jsonQuote(nativeID)\n57|\t}\n58|\treturn []byte(fmt.Sprintf(`{\"argv\":%s,\"cwd\":\"/tmp/ax\",\"env_names\":[],\"env_literals\":%s,\"native_session_id\":%s,\"profile_mapping\":%s,\"extensions\":{}}`,\n59|\t\targv, literals, native, jsonQuote(mapping)))\n60|}\n61|\n62|// validSpawnMapping returns the production YOLO flag for codex:\n63|// scaffolding for rows whose probe point is a different member,\n64|// so a mapping change cannot break them for the wrong reason.\n65|// Rows whose probe point IS the mapping construct their own\n66|// lengths and never call this.\n67|func validSpawnMapping(t *testing.T) string {\n68|\tt.Helper()\n69|\tmapping, err := provhost.ProfileMapping(\"codex\", provhost.ProfileYOLO)\n70|\tif err != nil {\n71|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"scaffolding: %v\", err)\n72|\t}\n73|\treturn mapping\n74|}\n75|\n76|// jsonQuote quotes a Go string as a JSON string literal.\n77|func jsonQuote(value string) string {\n78|\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"%q\", value)\n79|}\n80|\n(more lines below)"}}}
