{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c605","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0762f-28c8-71f3-b2cc-60a7b5a2a367"},"sequence":349,"recorded_at":1780531400000693,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"ce1e892e-3ef2-41ae-9338-dcad9ed9c1ee","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"ce1e892e-3ef2-41ae-9338-dcad9ed9c1ee","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"ce1e892e-3ef2-41ae-9338-dcad9ed9c1ee"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"271ae0c9-87da-48db-8282-9ab104f8a78e"},"task_id":"271ae0c9-87da-48db-8282-9ab104f8a78e","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"271ae0c9-87da-48db-8282-9ab104f8a78e","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-12-1\",\n  \"command\": \"git show 1296ecc --stat | head -n 20; echo ===; git show 1296ecc -- LOGBOOK.md | head -n 30; echo ===; ls internal/traceability/; sed -n '1,60p' internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck/main.go\",\n  \"description\": \"Inspect prior commit and tracecheck entry\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"commit 1296eccb0d19af3312b4a56ecb5dfc6f00c7d937\\nAuthor: Ivan Oparin <oparin@me.com>\\nDate:   Sun Sep 6 13:44:47 2026 +0400\\n\\n    TASK-260830-3bkz0c: TASK-260830-3bkz0c: prove-shared-environment-implementation-boundary\\n\\n LOGBOOK.md                                  |   9 +\\n internal/environ/census_test.go             | 381 +++++++++++++++++++++++\\n internal/environ/corpus_test.go             | 230 ++++++++++++++\\n internal/environ/decode.go                  | 456 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\\n internal/environ/doc.go                     |  48 +++\\n internal/environ/frame_agreement_test.go    | 398 ++++++++++++++++++++++++\\n internal/environ/identity_agreement_test.go | 228 ++++++++++++++\\n internal/environ/measure_agreement_test.go  | 238 +++++++++++++++\\n internal/environ/observation.go             | 387 +++++++++++++++++++++++\\n internal/environ/observation_test.go        | 267 ++++++++++++++++\\n internal/environ/tuple.go                   | 142 +++++++++\\n internal/environ/tuple_agreement_test.go    | 201 ++++++++++++\\n 12 files changed, 2985 insertions(+)\\n===\\ncommit 1296eccb0d19af3312b4a56ecb5dfc6f00c7d937\\nAuthor: Ivan Oparin <oparin@me.com>\\nDate:   Sun Sep 6 13:44:47 2026 +0400\\n\\n    TASK-260830-3bkz0c: TASK-260830-3bkz0c: prove-shared-environment-implementation-boundary\\n\\ndiff --git a/LOGBOOK.md b/LOGBOOK.md\\nindex fd2a806..e3fb383 100644\\n--- a/LOGBOOK.md\\n+++ b/LOGBOOK.md\\n@@ -5,6 +5,15 @@\\n \\n ## 2026-09-06\\n \\n+### 1347 — Shared-environment boundary leaf: one library plus fail-closed agreement battery\\n+- SCOPE: TASK-260830-3bkz0c (third/final leaf of STORY-260830-3drr2m). New package `internal/environ` (decode.go, tuple.go, observation.go, doc.go): single strict-frame decoder with string-walk surrogate semantics, rune measure, env-id/SemVer/arch grammars, exact six-member Tuple, §10.8.1 Environment Observation reusing the tuple model. Battery: census, frame/measure/tuple/identity agreement, observation. Frozen `sessadapter`/`dirnode` production untouched. Commit afdba1d (signed), PR #35 published.\\n+- FINDING: sessadapter+dirnode raw-scan surrogate gates REFUSE wire bodies carrying literal backslash-u text (`cursor` value `\\\\ud800` text) while environ+provhost+canonicaljson string-walk gates ACCEPT — proven via DecodeTuple/CheckScanRequest/Canonicalize. sessadapter `TestSurrogateGateAgreesWithCanonicalJSON` is one-directional (`!localRefuses && sharedRefuses`) and hides exactly this class. Ledgered in frame_agreement_test.go; unifying the frozen scanners is the recorded follow-up.\\n+- FINDING: truncated/malformed escapes refuse at the surrogate arm (raw scan) vs the syntax arm (string walk); wrong identity schema/version refuses at the member arm (provhost) vs the dispatch registry (canonicaljson). Same verdicts, different arms — ledgered per-judge, not papered over.\\n+- FINDING: battery caught its author's parity error — run-3 backslashes (`\\\\\\\\\\\\ud800`) are a real lone escape (odd runs escape, even runs quote), not divergence; row corrected to all-refuse before green.\\n+- EVIDENCE: attached TASK-260830-3bkz0c_boundary.md (7/7 AC rows with call sites) + TASK-260830-3bkz0c_mutation-log.md. Narrowing mutants 6/6 killed (N1/N2/N3/N4/N6 + token-preserving T1 raw-scan rewrite with census still green); D1 delete-only killed, scored as existence only. Tree sha-verified identical post-battery.\\n+- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (19 pkgs), environ `-race` exit 0, cover 76.1%, `go vet ./...` + `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0 (unchanged), catalog generate no-diff, `go build ./...` exit 0.\\n+- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off with CR published (review/landing are orchestrator steps).\\n+\\n ### 1035 — Directory-node leaf round-2 rework: rev1 B1/B2/B3 closed, 185-mutant battery\\n \\n - SCOPE: TASK-260830-ljkj8r round-2 rework (review-verdict-rev1, changes requested, B1–B3 blocking). Test-only additions inside `internal/dirnode/` (`bound_census_test.go`, `bounds_edge_test.go`, `query_operations_test.go`, `arm_identity_test.go`) plus four one-line fixture-surgery fixes (`query_test.go` unknown_field + missing caller, `manifest_test.go` missing member, `probe_test.go` missing member) and three edge extensions (findings 4097, cursor 1/1024 admission, projection bound edges). No production behavior change. Uncommitted per the CR-shape instruction.\\n===\\ncmd\\nownership.v0.5.0.json\\nreadme_figures_pin_test.go\\ntraceability_test.go\\ntraceability.go\\n// tracecheck is the headless CI entry point for AX specification-to-code\\n// ownership verification. It reports inventory coverage, not runtime support.\\npackage main\\n\\nimport (\\n\\t\\\"flag\\\"\\n\\t\\\"fmt\\\"\\n\\t\\\"io\\\"\\n\\t\\\"os\\\"\\n\\t\\\"strings\\\"\\n\\n\\t\\\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/traceability\\\"\\n)\\n\\nfunc main() {\\n\\tif err := run(os.Args[1:], os.Stdout); err != nil {\\n\\t\\tfmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, err)\\n\\t\\tos.Exit(1)\\n\\t}\\n}\\n\\nfunc run(arguments []string, stdout io.Writer) error {\\n\\tflags := flag.NewFlagSet(\\\"tracecheck\\\", flag.ContinueOnError)\\n\\tflags.SetOutput(io.Discard)\\n\\troot := flags.String(\\\"root\\\", \\\".\\\", \\\"repository root\\\")\\n\\tvar sections sectionFlags\\n\\tflags.Var(&sections, \\\"section\\\", \\\"assigned normative section or same-section range; repeat for multiple scopes\\\")\\n\\tif err := flags.Parse(arguments); err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn err\\n\\t}\\n\\tif flags.NArg() != 0 {\\n\\t\\treturn fmt.Errorf(\\\"unexpected positional arguments: %v\\\", flags.Args())\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\tvar report traceability.Report\\n\\tvar err error\\n\\tif len(sections) == 0 {\\n\\t\\treport, err = traceability.VerifyRepository(os.DirFS(*root))\\n\\t} else {\\n\\t\\treport, err = traceability.VerifyAssignedSections(os.DirFS(*root), sections)\\n\\t}\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn err\\n\\t}\\n\\tif _, err = fmt.Fprintf(\\n\\t\\tstdout,\\n\\t\\t\\\"traceability ok: contracts=%d normative_sections=%d acceptance_cases=%d fixtures=%d compatibility_contracts=%d assigned_scopes=%d\\\\n\\\",\\n\\t\\treport.Contracts,\\n\\t\\treport.NormativeSections,\\n\\t\\treport.AcceptanceCases,\\n\\t\\treport.Fixtures,\\n\\t\\treport.CompatibilityContracts,\\n\\t\\treport.AssignedScopes,\\n\\t); err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn err\\n\\t}\\n\\t// Coverage is printed as the measured ratio it was computed from. A gate\\n\\t// that reported \\\"sections owned\\\" would repeat the claim this line exists to\\n\\t// contradict.\\n\\t_, err = fmt.Fprintf(\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 6154,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1539,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
