{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c74f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0762f-28c8-71f3-b2cc-60a7b5a2a367"},"sequence":514,"recorded_at":1780531400001023,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"ce1e892e-3ef2-41ae-9338-dcad9ed9c1ee","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"ce1e892e-3ef2-41ae-9338-dcad9ed9c1ee","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"ce1e892e-3ef2-41ae-9338-dcad9ed9c1ee"},"call_id":"call_01a0763452457f508a7d7f8767c967cb","text":"Read text file `.temp/TASK-260830-3bkz0c/mut.sh`.\n1|#!/bin/zsh\n2|# usage: mut.sh <id> <python-mutation-script>\n3|# Applies one textual mutant to internal/environ, runs the environ\n4|# battery, reports KILLED/SURVIVED with the failing test names,\n5|# then restores the baseline. A mutant that leaves no textual\n6|# change reports NOT-APPLIED.\n7|set -u\n8|ROOT=/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-3drr2m/worktree\n9|BK=/tmp/env-baseline\n10|ID=$1; SCRIPT=$2\n11|restore() {\n12|  rm -rf \"$ROOT/internal/environ\"\n13|  cp -R \"$BK\" \"$ROOT/internal/environ\"\n14|}\n15|cd \"$ROOT\" || exit 9\n16|python3 \"$SCRIPT\" || { echo \"$ID APPLY-FAIL\"; restore; exit 8; }\n17|if diff -r -q \"$BK\" \"$ROOT/internal/environ\" >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n18|  echo \"$ID NOT-APPLIED (no textual change)\"; restore; exit 0\n19|fi\n20|OUT=$(cd \"$ROOT\" && timeout 400 go test ./internal/environ/ -count=1 2>&1)\n21|RC=$?\n22|if [ $RC -eq 0 ]; then echo \"$ID SURVIVED\"; else echo \"$ID KILLED\"; fi\n23|echo \"$OUT\" | grep -E 'FAIL: ' | head -14\n24|echo \"$OUT\" | grep -E '^(FAIL|ok) ' | head -4\n25|restore","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c751","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0762f-28c8-71f3-b2cc-60a7b5a2a367"},"sequence":515,"recorded_at":1780531400001025,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"ce1e892e-3ef2-41ae-9338-dcad9ed9c1ee","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"ce1e892e-3ef2-41ae-9338-dcad9ed9c1ee","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"ce1e892e-3ef2-41ae-9338-dcad9ed9c1ee"},"call_id":"call_01a0763452fa7aa2bb2cc6ae9e4785c7","text":"Read text file `.temp/TASK-260830-3bkz0c/prior-mutation-log.md`.\n1|# Mutation battery log — TASK-260830-3bkz0c\n2|\n3|Harness: `.temp/TASK-260830-3bkz0c/mut.sh` (scoped to\n4|`internal/environ`; restores from `/tmp/env-baseline` after every\n5|run). Each mutant applied by its named python script with a\n6|count==1 exact-match assertion (NOT-APPLIED if no textual\n7|change). Gate: `go test ./internal/environ/ -count=1`.\n8|Baseline tree sha: `.temp/TASK-260830-3bkz0c/pre-battery.sha`;\n9|post-battery sha identical (`diff` empty → TREE_IDENTICAL).\n10|\n11|## Narrowing mutants (gate stays present, admits exactly one member of the rejected class)\n12|\n13|| Mutant | Narrowing | Named failing test | Result |\n14||---|---|---|---|\n15|| N1 `n1_lowsurrogate.py`: drop the low-surrogate arm of the gate (admits lone lows, keeps refusing highs) | lone-low escapes | TestFrameAgreementAcrossFacades/bare_low_escape | KILLED |\n16|| N2 `n2_bytelength.py`: StringLength counts bytes, not runes | 128-char/256-byte values | TestStringMeasureCountsRunes/environ_helper | KILLED |\n17|| N3 `n3_tuplextensions.py`: tuple admits `extensions` member | one unknown member | TestTupleAgreementAcrossFacades/extensions_refused | KILLED |\n18|| N4 `n4_caplength.py`: capabilities length check `<` instead of `!=` (admits 9-key map) | ninth capability | TestDecodeEnvironmentObservation/ninth_capability_refused | KILLED |\n19|| N6 `n6_envunderscore.py`: env-id grammar admits `_` | underscore ids | TestSharedGrammarsAreOneLanguage | KILLED |\n20|| T1 `t1_rawscan.py`: gate keeps its name and refusal texts but matches `\\u` byte pairs without consuming `\\\\` pairs (raw-scan semantics) | escaped-backslash text | TestFrameAgreementAcrossFacades/escaped_backslash_{high,low,pair}_run2, _in_member_name, _nested (5 rows); TestSharedImplementationsAreCensused still PASSES under T1 | KILLED |\n21|\n22|T1 is the token-preserving attack on the census source-text\n23|gate: the symbol `HasLoneSurrogateEscape` stays defined, so a\n24|grep-level gate would pass, while the behavioral suite fails on\n25|exactly the escaped-backslash class. Census + behavior are\n26|complementary by construction, not by assertion.\n27|\n28|## Existence-only (not accepted as narrowing evidence)\n29|\n30|| Mutant | What it proves | Result |\n31||---|---|---|\n32|| D1 `d1_deletegate.py`: remove the surrogate-gate call (gate absent) | gate exists | KILLED (bare_high/low, high-followed-by-non-low, run3 rows) — existence only, excluded from the narrowing claim |\n33|\n34|## Totals\n35|\n36|Applied 7, killed 7. Narrowing kills 6 of 6 (N1, N2, N3, N4,\n37|N6, T1). Census-only kills 0 (no census-only mutant run).\n38|Over-applied (mutant fails to apply): 0. Survivors: none.\n39|Every surviving-mutant bound is therefore vacuous; no bound\n40|needs stating.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
