{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000ccf1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0762f-28c8-71f3-b2cc-60a7b5a2a367"},"sequence":1235,"recorded_at":1780531400002465,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"ce1e892e-3ef2-41ae-9338-dcad9ed9c1ee","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"ce1e892e-3ef2-41ae-9338-dcad9ed9c1ee","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"ce1e892e-3ef2-41ae-9338-dcad9ed9c1ee"},"terminal":"completed","text":"TASK-260830-3bkz0c is handed off to review (`to-review`, checklist 13/13).\n\nWhat this run did: no production changes — the `internal/environ` boundary library and battery from prior runs were independently re-verified on the committed candidate `1296ecc` (tree `292bc4242`, PR #35 head matches, frozen `sessadapter`/`dirnode` untouched, signature good).\n\nGates I ran myself, all exit 0: `go build`, `gofmt -l`, `go vet`, windows vet, `tracecheck`, full `go test ./... -count=1 -p 2` (19 packages), environ `-race` and `-cover` (76.1%). All 7 mutants re-killed (narrowing 6/6 including token-preserving T1, 0 survivors); tree verified restored-identical.\n\nKey finding: the CR rev1 validation failure (command 4/18) is a pre-existing `canonicaljson` wall-clock flake — `TestTransferManifestMaximumEntryGateIsLinear` budgets 2s, takes 1.14s alone but 3.5–4.6s under parallel load. Same-tree green runs exist, the leaf cannot cause it (no imports, empty diff), and weakening another story's timing gate would be a forced fit, so no code change was made. Full diagnosis is in the new outcome artifact `TASK-260830-3bkz0c_reverify.md`; recommendation is to re-run the CR suite.","reason":null}}
